00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:26.910
<i>Never gonna stop, never gonna stop</i>

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.040
<i>The feeling of love is happiness</i>

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.250
<i>You were not in pain, you were not in pain</i>

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.910
<i>Because we fall in love, there's sadness</i>

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.950
<i>Yeah, come on!</i>

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.250
<i>You gonna feel so</i>

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.250
<i>Yeah, come on!</i>

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:53.450
Chapter 3 Crimson

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:52.750
<i>Damn it... I...</i>

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:54.760
<i>I...</i>

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.960
<i>Like hell I'll ever give in!</i>

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:18.120
What a beauty!

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:29.540
<i>I'm going to do whatever it takes to
show that demon Vice Commander</i>

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.120
<i>the difference between how good
I am and how good that guy is!</i>

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:36.420
In these last few days,

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.340
the comings and goings of several
ronin have been witnessed.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:48.080
Take a quick look into Masuya,
the thrift shop on Shijo, for me.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:50.100
I understand. I will get to it right away.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.270
<i>Thrift shop... Masuya...</i>

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:56.530
Thanks for your continued business.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:00.110
Masuya

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.110
Mister Masuya?

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:07.580
Well, hello there. If it isn't Ms. Osen?

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.620
It certainly has been a
long time, hasn't it?

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.380
Not at all. So, what business
brings you here today?

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:19.910
Oh, well, I came to see if you
might have any small dressers,

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:22.120
but that was just my excuse.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:26.470
Truth is, I suddenly found
myself longing to see your face.

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:33.000
But your business seems
to be doing as well as ever.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.200
Oh, no, it's been so
dangerous around here lately,

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.370
business has all but dried up.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:39.320
Anyway, please, come on in for a bit.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:41.860
Dangerous, you say?

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:44.660
You know, the Mibu ronin.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.810
Though now, they call themselves
the Shinsengumi or some such

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:49.250
and seem to have a mighty
high opinion of themselves...

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.500
Goodness gracious, what <i>is </i>that?!

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.000
Maybe it's some kind of evil spirit?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.650
Don't look! It'll rot your eyes!

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.500
What the hell did you do that for?!

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.610
I'm trying to help you out here!
I even disguised myself as a girl...

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.070
Enough's enough!

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.080
First last night and now today!

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:25.280
I kept my mouth shut, reckoning you were just
a brat, but you had to go and push your luck!

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.200
Did you think I hadn't noticed?

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:32.620
What kind of page are you?

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.330
Quit sticking your nose
into other people's business

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.920
when you can't even carry out
your page duties to satisfaction!

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:42.840
You half-assed loser.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.720
You can't do anything
with what you've got now.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.020
Masuya

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:57.240
Poor thing, she's
still just a little child.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.750
Isn't anyone going to help her?

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:03.950
Don't be absurd! Those are ronin!
There's nothing to be done.

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:04.900
I...

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.830
C'mon, put up what ya
need to and we'll forgive ya.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:09.870
Money. We're talkin' money.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:14.250
Ya better not think ya can get away
scot-free after bumpin' into a samurai!

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.580
Excuse me, if you could not
do this in front of my shop...

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:23.340
She's a precious customer,
so if you would just...

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:26.450
What'd you just say?!

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:28.010
Aw, just leave 'im alone.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.680
Merchants're nothin' but
half-assed losers in the end.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.870
He can't do anythin' to us anyway.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:37.210
I... I...

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:01.700
What do you want?

00:06:01.700 --> 00:06:03.950
A friend of hers or somethin'?

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:06.910
Beat it, before ya get hurt!

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:09.930
I...

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.230
I'm not a half-assed loser!

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:25.730
Hey, Soji, there's something
that's been bugging me.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.200
I know you're off-duty,
but don't go around unarmed.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:30.660
What?

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:32.700
Don't "what" me!

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:36.200
When you're dressed like that,
you practically look like a girl!

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:40.870
Oh, what does it matter? It gets in
the way when playing tag and things.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:44.680
Come on, can't you look
a little more manly?

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.840
Mama!

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:52.290
Hey, Mama, there's a fight going
on over there! Let's go watch!

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:55.640
It's ronin going at each
other, right? It's dangerous.

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:56.910
No, no!

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:01.500
A little guy with pointy hair's
standing up to some bad samurai

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.060
who're picking on a little girl!

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:06.330
Unarmed at that! He's doing it unarmed!

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:10.370
Oh, child! There is no way
such silliness could be true!

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:11.750
Come on, we're going home!

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.070
Mama!

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.660
Pointy...

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:16.950
hair?

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.700
No way, it can't be.

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:23.200
Yeah, there's just no way.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:30.660
But Tetsunosuke doesn't have a
sword of his own yet, does he?

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:34.970
Soji, if it were you, how would you
fight unarmed against a sword?

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:38.120
Well, let me think.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:41.440
I suppose there are a number
of ways to go about it, but...

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:44.230
Masuya

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:43.760
I think I'd use my feet first!

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:47.480
Damn brat!

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:58.830
<i>This is bad. If he keeps
carrying on like this...</i>

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:00.450
You damn brat!

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:06.840
All right, that's a good boy.
Don't move now.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:11.300
Here, this cute lil' girl's face
is goin' to get all cut up.

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:17.600
Well then, better give ya
the punishment ya deserve!

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:28.480
Now!

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:36.780
I thought you were just
a brat, but it seems...

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:39.790
that ya don't need to be cut any slack.

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:49.750
Please wait.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.550
You'll reveal the nature of your job.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:00.060
My, my, how dangerous.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.620
This may be a game,

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:04.940
but I cannot approve of drawing
swords on a public street.

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:06.490
Who the hell're you?

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.490
Oki...

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.230
Hold it right there.

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:12.730
We aren't anyone whose
names are worth mentioning.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:14.620
Hey, even the little one?!

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:17.030
Like you're one to talk?!

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:23.040
Hey! I don't know who the hell
ya are, but we've got the brat!

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:25.500
So ya better stay outta...

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:30.210
You're pointing your sword
in the wrong direction, mister.

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:36.500
And the big one too?

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:41.430
All right! You guys, leave the rest
to us and get on out of here.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:44.830
Tetsu, this way!

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:46.660
Oh, okay!

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:53.290
You bastards...

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.280
Draw! I'll cut ya to pieces!

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:59.540
Sorry, but I'm not too hot with a sword.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:00.200
So...

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.660
you'll have to let me use this instead!

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:07.540
Quit messin' with us!

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:16.090
You just narrowly escaped death.

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:25.390
Starting tomorrow, you better bow
to the shop curtain before entering!

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:28.980
Hey, Sano, pull your punches a little.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.660
Holy...!

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:35.110
Scaring me like that!

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:38.910
What's the matter, Shinpachi?
Want some help?

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:40.320
Don't be silly.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:42.200
Die!

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:44.910
You know...

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.790
It's too late to beg for yer life!

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.580
No, that's not it.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:51.710
You think you can beat me
with a push like that?

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:53.960
Shoo...

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:00.950
Too bad for you.

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:05.200
I might not look it,
but I'm actually pretty good.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:07.700
Hey, did you just kill him?

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:10.100
Moron, I hit him with the
back of the sword. The back.

00:11:10.410 --> 00:11:12.520
All right, one to go!

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:15.690
What?

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:17.360
Wha...?

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:24.120
We certainly ran quite a ways, didn't we?

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.290
We should be far enough
that you'll be fine.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:30.460
Tetsu, leave the rest to us
and escape with the girl.

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.790
No! I also...

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:34.330
You also what?

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.460
Mr. Okita!

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:03.250
For this commotion to have
happened in spite of my being there,

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:05.120
I am very sorry.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.000
No, that's fine.

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:09.910
You carried out your mission well.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:11.660
Report your findings to me.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:12.750
Yes, sir.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.620
The three men that started the commotion...

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:20.050
From their accent, there is no
question that they are from Choshu.

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:25.120
Two were defeated by some passing ronin,
who tried to help the girl,

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:27.120
and fled the scene.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.930
The remaining man...

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:36.370
Passing ronin?

00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:39.940
It was unfortunate that
Soji was one of them.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:43.400
However, we now know something interesting.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:46.200
The demeanor of those men

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.870
is the very picture of countryside samurai.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:54.000
Yes, if they had been lurking in Kyoto
for any length of time and knew of us,

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:55.920
they would not have behaved as they did.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:57.620
Most likely...

00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:00.800
they are recent arrivals in Kyoto.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:05.200
And even after such a disturbance
right in front of their shop,

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:07.800
Masuya hasn't reported a word of it.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.870
Shall we bring him in?

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:21.650
No, not yet.

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:28.160
If they're just gathering impetuous youths
to have a gawk at Kyoto, that's one thing,

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:31.660
but knowing their love of festivals,

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:35.710
they're bound to be planning
some kind of crazy show.

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:37.250
Festivals?

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:41.080
Yeah, a festival named "revolution."

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.000
Even if we brought Masuya in now,

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:45.090
he's unlikely to know anything worthwhile.

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.830
Feed them more, fatten them up.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.560
We can devour them...

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:55.690
afterwards.

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:01.250
However, due to this incident,

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:05.120
they will likely act even
more covertly than before.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:06.700
Probably.

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:09.290
The responsibility is entirely mine.

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:11.700
I have not only hindered our investigation,

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:13.910
but also roused the enemy's wariness.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.910
I will accept any punishment
you see fit to sentence me to.

00:14:25.910 --> 00:14:29.510
I will not punish anyone in
connection with this incident.

00:14:30.330 --> 00:14:33.930
The responsibility for it all will
be mine as the Vice Commander.

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:34.910
Yes, sir.

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:43.270
Yamazaki...

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:45.530
Am I...

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:48.160
being too soft?

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:54.350
There can be no mistake
in anything that you do.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:10.350
<i>It's the first time I've ever gotten mad.</i>

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:15.080
To think you made that Mr. Yamazaki mad...

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:17.810
You really are impressive.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:21.040
Well, it's all good, isn't it?

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:23.810
No matter how you look at it,
those men were in the wrong.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.050
Why...

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:28.360
Why did you kill him?!

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:30.700
We'd already won at that point!

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:35.200
You could've let him go or
taken him captive or something!

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:36.220
Why?!

00:15:41.700 --> 00:15:44.370
That man was unlucky.

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:45.340
What?

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:48.450
He raised his sword, not against
the man disguising himself as a ronin,

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:51.760
but against Okita of the Shinsengumi.

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:54.970
What do you mean by that?

00:15:54.970 --> 00:16:00.160
I believe there are probably people
from Choshu hiding at Masuya.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:02.870
Those people must have been quite horrified

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:08.110
when some of their friends raised
that commotion in front of the shop.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:14.110
However, the Shinsengumi could not
mobilize to quell that commotion.

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:16.580
For if we had,

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:22.000
all the people from Choshu
hiding there would surely have fled.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:23.540
Are you saying...?

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:30.960
And so, we tried to help you merely
as ronin who happened by, but...

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:35.970
Because I called out your name?

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:38.000
Because I...

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:43.000
It is not your fault.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:47.410
In a way different from that
Choshu man, you were also unlucky.

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:49.230
That is all there is to it.

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:51.540
That's all?

00:16:51.540 --> 00:16:55.900
A man was killed, and
that's all there is to it?

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:57.630
Yes...

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:03.540
Even people of Choshu are
someone's children! Someone's parents!

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.330
And you're saying...

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.840
I am not a child of man.

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:14.170
I am a demon's child.

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:22.460
Tetsu, there is something
I must impart to you.

00:17:25.450 --> 00:17:27.330
The Strictures of the Shinsengumi.

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:31.660
Truly a demon's code that
Mr. Hijikata came up with.

00:17:31.660 --> 00:17:33.610
These are our proscriptions.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:45.120
Strictures of the Shinsengumi.

00:17:34.200 --> 00:17:37.790
One, you must not stray
from the samurai's code.

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:41.330
Two, desertion is not permitted.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:45.120
Three, you will not raise
funds without permission.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:49.410
Four, you will not take up litigious
matters without permission.

00:17:49.410 --> 00:17:52.570
Five, private conflicts are not permitted.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:57.430
Those who defy these articles shall
be sentenced to commit seppuku,

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:00.850
without fail.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.120
By the samurai's code,

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:10.450
failing to strike down the
enemy is not permitted.

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:14.750
Drawing your sword as a
member of the Shinsengumi

00:18:14.750 --> 00:18:18.530
means that either you or
your enemy will inevitably die.

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:25.880
Working as a page was the one
and only way to avoid that risk.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.790
What kind of page are you?

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:33.250
Quit sticking your nose
into other people's business.

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:37.250
However, you are the one
who must make the choice.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:39.250
If you wish to become stronger...

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.660
If you wish to have your revenge...

00:18:41.660 --> 00:18:44.720
Abandon your humanity
and take up the sword.

00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:05.760
Honestly! Leaving all these ledgers
to collect dust this whole time...

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:08.390
Oh, hey, Tetsunosuke.

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:11.230
Won't you help me carry these?

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:16.000
Hey, I'm going to drop them!

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:21.700
I... really am...

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:23.110
a half-assed loser.

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:24.350
Tetsu...

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:31.330
Good grief. What did you do this time?

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:35.920
Masuya

00:20:36.110 --> 00:20:39.000
So, one of our comrades...

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:43.290
Yes. It was just some horseplay at first,

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:47.510
but they went a little too
far in their tomfoolery.

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:51.370
I can understand their
excitement in coming to Kyoto,

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:54.660
but picking on a child is...
Well, you know...

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:55.980
Unforgivable.

00:20:56.950 --> 00:20:58.700
They'll be executed.

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:00.440
No, that's...

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:03.390
Apparently, that's the final decision.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:09.620
But well, that was to be expected.

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:13.290
As a patriot who reveres the
Emperor and favors exclusionism,

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:17.640
it is essential to have a proud spirit.

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:29.850
Master!

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:31.450
Master Yoshida!

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:36.230
A faithful soul to offer one's master...

00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:40.730
the strength to be a sword that
will bring down the Shogunate...

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:46.080
and most beautiful of all,

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:53.100
a brilliant madness that burns
as brightly as crimson blood.

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:07.910
<i>Gripping the microphone tight,
the hit parade's on parade</i>

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:11.450
<i>Hey, Jimmy, how you feeling?</i>

00:22:11.450 --> 00:22:15.790
<i>Quite the gentleman when he's off stage</i>

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:19.520
<i>Hey, Jimmy, a generous spirit too!</i>

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:23.400
<i>Being such an honest guy,
even his life's plain</i>

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:27.290
<i>Keep building it up patiently</i>

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:31.290
<i>May your dreams come true honestly</i>

00:22:31.290 --> 00:22:35.120
<i>Let's go for it again today, Jimmy</i>

00:22:37.160 --> 00:22:40.660
<i>You got to fight for your money!
How you feeling, Jimmy?</i>

00:22:40.660 --> 00:22:44.590
<i>You got to fight for your dream,
it's all too much</i>

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:48.500
<i>You got to fight for your money!
How you feeling, Jimmy?</i>

